// Nodes: sources 0..n-1, targets n..n+m-1, root n+m.
// Arcs stored for the spanning tree via parent pointers.
// Non-tree arcs are implicit (all source-target pairs).
//
// We follow the standard "network simplex for the transportation problem"
// (Bonneel et al. 2011 / LEMON style) with:
//   - initial basis: each source connected to cheapest target, plus artificial
//     arcs from root to targets to satisfy supply, and root connected to one source.
// Actually a simpler feasible basis: connect every source and target to root
// with artificial high-cost arcs, then optimize. That's the "all artificial" start.
//
// To match POT exactly we may need the same pivot rule. First just get a correct
// optimal plan and measure speed.
#include <cstdint>
#include <vector>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstring>
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <chrono>
#include <random>
#include <limits>

